From d4f1bc486466bc9ac5ac8f96c9f70822e08f3cbc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 01:39:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): preserve owner-routed foreign session tiles
 [daveey]

Remove the ambient identity guard and wrong-backend resume classification.
Keep conservative restored-dead-tile deletion checks and owner-scoped routing.

Why chain:
- Correctly routed foreign tiles lost their runtime on ambient connection
  refresh: startTileBackendIdentityGuard unconditionally compared owner to
  ambient and deleted runtimeId (session-tile.tsx, base lines 149-162).
- The guard assumed a tile must use the primary backend. cd2915ac6c added
  that assumption alongside the valid registry-primary boot fix, but the
  tile delegate now explicitly routes REST/RPC through the tile owner.
- Recovery also stalled: owner 404s became WRONG_BACKEND_TILE_ERROR and
  the reconnect effect specifically refused to clear that error.
- Detection gap: old tests asserted foreign tiles must be unbound; resolver
  and delegate tests did not run the controller's connection subscription.
  The new integration imports real controller/open/resolver/store/delegate
  and mounts SessionTilePane for retry/reconnect (transport and ChatView
  rendering mocked). On base: 4 failures, 1 pass; fixed: 5 pass.

Preserve workspace bucket changes: changing connection IDs intentionally
hides/restores runtime-less persisted tiles (session-states.ts:1502-1525).
Test that restoration is unpoisoned and owner resume succeeds; same-scope
connection refresh/baseURL/token changes keep the existing foreign runtime.

Verified: targeted vitest 10 files / 255 tests (including original Electron
primary-startup/remote-route controls), eslint touched files, separate tsc.
No live checkout changes, app restart, push or deployment.
